message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Assumed infrastructure: what do instruction-tuned LLMs take for granted? A pre-registered audit of four small open models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Savadogo"
    given-names: "Modeste"
repository-code: "https://github.com/modestesavadogo/assumed-infrastructure"
url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/SavadogoModeste/assumed-infrastructure-audit"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - large language models
  - cultural bias
  - evaluation
  - infrastructure
  - pre-registration
  - audit
abstract: >-
  Four small instruction-tuned chat models (Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507, Phi-4-mini-instruct, Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct,
  Qwen3-1.7B) answer practical-advice requests under ten context conditions. The study measures, with a frozen keyword
  lexicon, next-token probes and a blind manual audit, whether the models assume steady electricity, fast internet and
  international cards, and how deeply they adapt to a stated place or explicit constraints. Code, inputs and audit
  materials are MIT / CC BY 4.0; raw outputs are in the companion Hugging Face dataset.
